[0.001, "o", "\u001b[32m succeeded in 0ms:\u001b[0m\r\n# Decision: should we keep paying for the on-call paging tool? (synthetic demo input)\r\n\r\nThis scenario is invented for a skill demo. The team and numbers are not real.\r\n\r\n- Team: 6 engineers share a weekly on-call rotation for one web app.\r\n- Current paging tool costs $3,600 per year. Renewal is due in 30 days.\r\n- Alternative: route alerts to a shared chat channel for free and drop the tool.\r\n- Last quarter there were 14 production alerts; 3 were real outages, the rest were noise.\r\n- One outage last year was noticed late (about 40 minutes) because nobody saw a chat message at night.\r\n- Rough revenue during business hours is about $2,000 per hour; nights are much lower.\r\n- We would cancel if the expected yearly cost of slower response is clearly below $3,600.\r\n\r\n"]
[27.091, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mcodex\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\nThe central scenario comes out below $3,600, but plausible assumptions also put the cost well above it. The key unknown is how much additional outage time chat would cause and what each added hour would cost. I’ll make those assumptions explicit; the 40-minute incident establishes a risk, but doesn’t tell us how often it occurs.\r\n\r\n"]
[72.732, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/bin/zsh -lc 'mkdir -p memos'"]
