[0.022, "o", "\u001b[1mpatch:\u001b[0m completed\r\n\u001b[2m/private/tmp/skills-demo-htma-measure/home/htma-measure-demo/memos/paging-tool-measurement.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "diff --git a/memos/paging-tool-measurement.md b/memos/paging-tool-measurement.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..621a891f3bcc3d6e71d3c99941b1816bc0ad7f70\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/memos/paging-tool-measurement.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@\r\n+# Paging tool renewal measurement brief\r\n+\r\n+The illustrative central estimate of added loss from switching to chat is **about $1,500 per year**, with a **provisional subjective 90% range of $0–$60,000 per year**. This crosses the $3,600 renewal threshold substantially. The supplied evidence does **not** establish that cancellation is clearly cheaper. Measure the response-time difference before renewal; retain paging if that uncertainty remains unresolved.\r\n+\r\n+**Date:** 2026-11-05  \r\n+**Scope:** Synthetic demo; next 12 months after the renewal decision. Estimate incremental direct revenue loss caused by slower response under chat compared with the existing paging tool. All dollar figures use the scenario's dollar unit. No real team, vendor, o"]
[0.000, "o", "r private financial data is implied.\r\n+\r\n+## 1. Question made precise\r\n+\r\n+- **Decision:** Pay $3,600 for another year of paging, or use the free shared chat channel.\r\n+- **Quantity:** Expected annual direct revenue loss attributable to additional outage time under chat.\r\n+- **Unit and horizon:** Dollars per year, over the next 12 months.\r\n+- **Threshold:** $3,600 per year. Cancel only if expected incremental loss is clearly below this amount.\r\n+- **Operational interpretation of “clearly”:** Use an upper 90% uncertainty bound below $3,600 as a proposed evidence standard. The user supplied the threshold, but did not specify this confidence standard.\r\n+- **Cost of being wrong:** Unnecessary renewal costs up to $3,600 in avoidable subscription expense; mistaken cancellation may cause losses beyond the subscription saving. Customer, contractual, recovery-labor, and reputational costs are unquantified.\r\n+- **Estimate mode:** Budget allowance for uncertain incremental operational loss. This is a conditional for"]
[0.000, "o", "ecast, not a vendor quote or an estimate of a missing private actual.\r\n+\r\n+## 2. Short answer\r\n+\r\n+| Item | Estimate |\r\n+| --- | --- |\r\n+| Central expected annual loss | $1,440 calculated; report as about $1,500 |\r\n+| Working 90% uncertainty interval | $0–$60,000 per year |\r\n+| Confidence | Subjective and provisional; weak evidence for the interval's coverage |\r\n+| Central net saving from cancellation | $3,600 − $1,440 = $2,160 per year |\r\n+| Action implication | Central estimate favors cancellation, but the stated “clearly below” condition is not met |\r\n+\r\n+This interval describes uncertainty about the **expected annual loss**, not the distribution of losses realized in a particular year. There is no defensible estimate of the probability that cancellation is cheaper from the available evidence alone.\r\n+\r\n+## 3. Priors and sources\r\n+\r\n+| Source / anchor | Value | Quality and relevance | Treatment |\r\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n+| Synthetic decision input, local `decision.md` | 6 engineers; weekly rot"]
[0.000, "o", "ation; $3,600 annual price; renewal in 30 days | Highest relevance to the scenario; invented and not independently verified | Supplied facts within this demo |\r\n+| Same input: last quarter | 14 alerts, including 3 outages and 11 noise alerts | Direct small sample; calendar quarter and seasonality unspecified | Annualized anchor: 12 outages and 56 alerts; not a reliable forecast by itself |\r\n+| Same input: historical incident | About 40 minutes of late discovery at night | Demonstrates a missed-chat mechanism; only one selected example | Does not establish frequency or paging's counterfactual performance |\r\n+| Same input: revenue | About $2,000/hour during business hours; nights much lower | Relevant but rough; gross revenue is not necessarily permanently lost revenue | Anchors loss scale, not a confirmed outage loss rate |\r\n+| Analyst assumptions below | Frequency, causal delay, and effective loss rate | Lowest quality; explicit judgment rather than measured parameters | Broad conditional scenarios, to replac"]
[0.000, "o", "e with observations |\r\n+\r\n+No external benchmarks or current external factual claims are used. Web research would not resolve this invented app's response behavior or revenue loss. There is no comparable-case dataset beyond the supplied quarter and incident. Local vendor discounts are irrelevant because the subscription price is supplied and the alternative is free.\r\n+\r\n+## 4. Decomposition\r\n+\r\n+Use:\r\n+\r\n+**Annual incremental loss = N × p × d × L**\r\n+\r\n+Here, `N` is outages/year; `p` is the fraction where chat causes additional revenue-relevant outage time; `d` is mean additional hours for those affected outages; and `L` is effective permanently lost revenue per added hour, weighted by when those delays occur. This is a scenario model: the conditional averages must reflect the same affected incidents. Multiplying unrelated marginal averages could misstate loss.\r\n+\r\n+| Component | Low scenario | Central scenario | High scenario | Confidence / basis | What would tighten it |\r\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --"]
[0.001, "o", "- | --- |\r\n+| N: real outages/year | 4 | 12 | 24 | Weak; central annualizes 3 in one quarter; bounds are judgment, not a count confidence interval | Prior 12–24 months of incident records |\r\n+| p: fraction affected by chat | 0 | 0.40 | 0.80 | Very weak; one missed message supplies no denominator or comparative rate | Paired chat and paging acknowledgments by time of day |\r\n+| d: extra outage hours per affected incident | 0 | 0.50 | 2.00 | Very weak; 40-minute discovery example informs scale, but does not measure net outage extension | Alert, acknowledgment, mitigation, and recovery timestamps |\r\n+| L: effective lost dollars per added hour | 0 | 600 | 1,500 | Very weak; judgment below supplied $2,000 business-hour revenue; allows lower night revenue, partial impact, and later recapture | Revenue by hour, affected share, and permanently lost share |\r\n+| N × p × d × L: dollars/year | 0 | 1,440 | 57,600 | Conditional scenario arithmetic | Joint incident-level delay and loss estimates |\r\n+\r\n+The central `p`, "]
[0.000, "o", "`d`, and `L` are **elicitation placeholders**, not inferred private facts. Noise is excluded from the outage count; its potential effect on attention is part of `p`. Six engineers sharing a rotation does not establish that six people monitor chat at night. The paging tool's actual effectiveness is also unknown; it is not assumed to prevent every delay.\r\n+\r\n+The estimate excludes subscription cost itself, because it is the comparison threshold. It also excludes unmeasured labor, customer, and contractual effects. Treat those as a separate decision consideration rather than silently assigning them zero in a total-cost claim.\r\n+\r\n+## 5. Calibrated range and threshold sensitivity\r\n+\r\n+The reported **$0–$60,000** interval rounds outward from the $0 and $57,600 joint scenarios. The component columns are coherent scenarios, **not individual 90% intervals**. Multiplying component bounds does not establish probabilistic coverage.\r\n+\r\n+The 90% label is a provisional subjective coverage judgment, conditional on broadl"]
[0.000, "o", "y similar app economics and operations. It is not statistically validated calibration. The lower bound includes no incremental causal harm. The upper scenario allows twice the annualized outage count, frequent chat delays, two extra hours per affected outage, and losses weighted toward valuable hours. Longer overnight delays, clustered failures, or unpriced customer effects could exceed it. No Monte Carlo simulation is warranted with these weakly elicited inputs.\r\n+\r\n+Equivalent-bet check: do not claim a verified 1-in-20 chance of exceeding $60,000. An owner would need to review whether that upper-tail belief is credible before treating this as a calibrated operational forecast. The current evidence supports a broad decision aid, with low confidence in exact endpoints.\r\n+\r\n+At 12 outages/year, cancellation breaks even at **$300 additional loss per outage**, averaged across all outages. Equivalent limits are:\r\n+\r\n+| Effective loss rate during extra downtime | Break-even added downtime across the year |\r\n+| ---"]
[0.000, "o", " | ---: |\r\n+| $2,000/hour, supplied business-hour revenue anchor assuming all is lost | 1.8 hours |\r\n+| $600/hour, central effective loss assumption | 6 hours |\r\n+\r\n+Holding central `N`, `p`, and `L` fixed, mean extra outage time of **1.25 hours per affected incident** reaches $3,600/year. Alternatively, 12 outages × 50% affected × 40/60 extra hours × $1,000/hour = **$4,000/year**. That crossing scenario uses an assumed causal 40-minute extension; the historical discovery delay does not prove such an extension.\r\n+\r\n+## 6. Value of information\r\n+\r\n+| Rank | Uncertainty | Measurement before renewal | Decision impact |\r\n+| ---: | --- | --- | --- |\r\n+| 1 | Joint additional outage duration and lost revenue under chat | Review available incidents over the prior 12 months: time of day, chat visibility, page delivery, acknowledgment, recovery, affected revenue, and likely response without paging | Directly estimates incremental dollars per outage and can move the answer across $300/outage |\r\n+| 2 | Overnight chat "]
[0.000, "o", "response and paging's advantage | Retain paging during a short shadow comparison; use a small set of prearranged test alerts across shifts and record acknowledgment times | Tests the missed-chat mechanism; tests must not be treated as proof of real-outage response or recovery |\r\n+| 3 | Outage frequency and clustering | Classify prior 12–24 months of alerts; separate outages from noise and note operating changes | Replaces extrapolation from only 3 outages |\r\n+\r\n+**Numeric expected value of information: unknown.** The probability of a changed decision, measurement quality, effort cost, and costs of the two errors are not supplied sufficiently to calculate it. The ranking is qualitative.\r\n+\r\n+Use existing records first. At the annualized rate, a 30-day observation period would contain only about one real outage on average, so a quiet month cannot establish safety. Stop measuring once a credible upper bound on annual incremental loss is below $3,600, or a credible lower bound is above it. If the interval still"]
[0.000, "o", " crosses the threshold near renewal, additional low-information monitoring has not satisfied the cancellation condition.\r\n+\r\n+## 7. What would move the estimate\r\n+\r\n+- **Up:** Frequent overnight misses, hours-long acknowledgment gaps, incident delays concentrated in valuable hours, sustained revenue loss, or evidence that paging reliably shortens recovery.\r\n+- **Down:** Reliable staffed chat coverage, similar chat and paging acknowledgment times, little effect of detection on recovery, substantially lower permanently lost revenue, or fewer real outages.\r\n+- **No longer decision-relevant:** Remaining uncertainty cannot move the annual incremental cost across $3,600. For example, sufficiently credible evidence that it stays below $300 per outage at a well-supported 12 outages/year would support cancellation.\r\n+\r\n+## 8. Recommendation\r\n+\r\n+**Do not cancel on the supplied evidence alone.** The central estimate favors cancellation, but uncertainty spans both decisions widely. Use the remaining 30 days to inspect i"]
[0.000, "o", "ncident records and compare acknowledgment behavior. If those measurements do not establish loss clearly below $3,600, retain paging under the user's stated decision rule. Renewal is a conservative choice under that rule, not a demonstrated positive-ROI result.\r\n+\r\n+## Sources\r\n+\r\n+- [Synthetic scenario supplied by the user](../decision.md).\r\n+- [HTMA skill workflow](../../.agents/skills/htma-measure/SKILL.md).\r\n+- [Measurement brief template](../../.agents/skills/htma-measure/assets/measurement-brief-template.md), [method map](../../.agents/skills/htma-measure/references/method-map.md), and [output rubric](../../.agents/skills/htma-measure/references/output-rubric.md).\r\n+- All unsourced numeric scenario parameters are explicitly labeled analyst assumptions in Section 4.\r\n+\r\n+## HTMA_RESULT\r\n+\r\n+```json\r\n+{\r\n+  \"quantity\": \"Expected annual incremental direct revenue loss from switching from paging to shared chat\",\r\n+  \"unit\": \"dollars per year\",\r\n+  \"low_90\": 0,\r\n+  \"central\": 1500,\r\n+  \"high_90\": 60000,\r\n+  "]
[0.000, "o", "\"confidence\": \"Provisional subjective 90% uncertainty interval; weak evidence and no validated empirical coverage; conditional on stated assumptions\",\r\n+  \"decision_threshold\": 3600,\r\n+  \"threshold_implication\": \"Central estimate favors cancellation, but the interval crosses $3,600 widely. Cancellation is not clearly cheaper; retain paging if targeted measurement does not resolve uncertainty before renewal.\",\r\n+  \"top_uncertainty_driver\": \"Additional revenue-relevant outage hours caused by chat, jointly with the effective loss rate during those hours\",\r\n+  \"estimate_status\": \"estimated\",\r\n+  \"blocking_missing_inputs\": [],\r\n+  \"assumed_target\": \"Budget allowance forecast of incremental direct revenue loss over the next 12 months in the supplied synthetic scenario\",\r\n+  \"next_measurement_step\": \"Review available incidents from the prior 12 months for paired chat/page acknowledgment and recovery timestamps, time-of-day revenue, and the likely extra outage duration without paging; estimate incremental loss per ou"]
[0.000, "o", "tage against the $300 break-even anchor.\"\r\n+}\r\n+```\r\n\r\n"]
[6.918, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\r\nimport json, pathlib, re\r\np = pathlib.Path('memos/paging-tool-measurement.md')\r\ns = p.read_text()\r\nr = json.loads(re.search(r'\"'```json'\"\\\\n(.*?)\\\\n\"'```'\"', s, re.S).group(1))\r\nassert r['estimate_status'] == 'estimated' and not r['blocking_missing_inputs']\r\nassert r['low_90'] <= r['central'] <= r['high_90']\r\nassert 12 * .4 * .5 * 600 == 1440\r\nassert 24 * .8 * 2 * 1500 == 57600\r\nfor target in re.findall(r'\\\\]\\\\(([\"'^)]+)'\"\\\\)', s):\r\n    assert (p.parent / target).exists(), target\r\nprint('Verified JSON consistency, scenario arithmetic, and all local source links.')\r\nPY\"\u001b[0m"]
